# Documentation stays current

Never finish a code change with stale documentation. Update the matching pages in the same change. Do not defer docs to a later task.

## Two portals

1. **User help center** (signed-in users): `src/docs/content/*.md`, `src/docs/catalog.js`, `src/docs/content/index.js`
2. **Engineering portal**: `README.md` and `docs/`

Shared product, API, permission, data-model, and limitation docs live in this frontend `docs/` portal even when the change is in `payroll-backend`.

## When to update

Update whenever the change affects screens, copy, navigation, routes, permissions, workflows, APIs, entities, schema, configuration, integrations, schedulers, operations, or user-visible UI.

Skip only no-behavior edits (formatting, comments, unused-code cleanup). If you skip, say so in the reply.

## Where to write

| Change | User help | Engineering |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Screen or workflow | matching `src/docs/content/*.md` | `docs/features/` |
| Route, nav, permission | `find-your-way.md` plus the screen article | `docs/reference/routes-and-permissions.md` |
| New screen | new article + `catalog.js` + `content/index.js` | feature page + routes |
| API or auth | only if a user step changed | `docs/reference/api-reference.md`, security |
| Entity or schema | glossary if a term changed | `docs/architecture/data-model.md` |
| Tokens or shell UI | help chrome only if readers see it | `docs/architecture/design-system.md` |
| Config, deploy, scheduler | — | operations pages + backend `docs/` |
| Gap found or fixed | FAQ if users hit it | `docs/operations/known-limitations.md` |

Treat current executable code as truth. Label intended behavior vs implemented. Keep page metadata: Audience, Purpose, Last verified, Source of truth. Never add credentials, tokens, personal data, salary data, or production endpoints.

Run `npm run docs:check` before completion.
